LOGBOOK.md:678:- ADDRESS: Resolver results with a non-empty IPv6 zone are discarded before unmapping, accepted-result byte credit, family/socket admission, or send. An all-scoped result set closes its original bounded reservation with zero descriptors/sends and zero retained scheduler/registry resources; a later in-cap unzoned IPv6 result is selected byte-exactly without zone rewriting. The system socket seam also rejects zoned IPv6 defensively.
LOGBOOK.md:687:- REWORK: Domain sends now reserve socketless association capacity and an exact generation/incarnation token before resolver admission. A fixed worker pool and fixed queued-job/completion credit bound copied names, payloads, inspected/accepted results, retained result bytes, deadlines, and concurrent lookups; `Send` returns `pendingResolution` without blocking the event-loop caller. Completion attaches a family socket only through the original token.
LOGBOOK.md:722:- CORRECTION: `Degraded(g)` no longer requires a null registration in every degraded substate. Plain degraded requires registration null/phase `none`; Waiting requires exactly one current `reprobeWaiting` timer registration; Running requires exactly one current `reprobeAttempt` registration with a current attempt generation. Each branch retains current `BaseReady`, null active relay, closed UDP, and invalidated retired associations before publishing `(1,1,0)`.
LOGBOOK.md:727:- READINESS: `ValidatedRelayCandidate` is now an internal current-registration proof that explicitly requires `activeRelayGeneration=null`, closed UDP admission, and no application association. T04 retains only this inactive proof with `activation_ready`; T07/T21/T26 are the atomic bind-promote-open publication points and must re-prove target-state `Full(g)`.
LOGBOOK.md:753:- PROVENANCE REWORK: Release entry points now require offline-provisioned official Go and Syft archives retained beside their installed tools. They recheck the accepted host-specific archive hash, canonical path-free receipt, installed archive members, exact Go 1.26.5 host identity with `GOTOOLCHAIN=local`, and Syft 1.48.0 commit `3e2bc6ed095f7ec1a415fb38cfe1c319e95dfed6`; missing, older/newer, wrong-platform, wrong-commit, wrong-checksum, auto-toolchain, and version-only inputs fail closed.
LOGBOOK.md:775:- PRIVACY INCIDENT: An early live environment-inspection output included local device/account identifiers. No identifier was copied into research, raw measurement, evidence-bundle, board-note, or downstream artifacts; the automatically retained runner log was sanitized to generic redaction markers before outcome publication. Future environment rows for this task are limited to hardware model, architecture, OS, tool version, and source revision.
LOGBOOK.md:785:- DECISION: `TCPAdmissionRegistry` is one generation-scoped mutex authority for pending handshakes, authenticated flows, concurrent channel opens, owned channels, fixed directional queue capacity, live buffered bytes, and phase counts. All ceilings and the measured-safe/HEV evidence gates are caller-injected; denial is synchronous, retains no waiter, maps to SOCKS5 `REP=01`, and explicitly prohibits an SSH open. Reservation identifiers are monotonically allocated without reuse and fail closed with finite `identifier_capacity` pressure before `UInt64` wrap.
LOGBOOK.md:791:- DECISION: `ReluxTunnelCore` now owns a candidate-neutral local nonblocking byte-stream/readiness seam and one structured full-duplex pump. Each direction retains exactly one current `Data` plus offset; no next read occurs until that buffer drains. Caller-injected chunk/write/fairness/no-progress limits are validated, and a shared non-waiting reservation actor caps aggregate pump-owned bytes across concurrent flows without a capacity queue.
LOGBOOK.md:809:- FIX: Both iOS and macOS `VPNHostSession` adapters now catch synchronous `NETunnelProviderSession.startTunnel(options:)` errors and translate them through the existing `VPNPreferencePlatformError` model before crossing into `VPNSessionController`. Public `NEVPNError.configurationInvalid`, `.configurationDisabled`, and `.connectionFailed` retain their stable results; every other `NSError` retains its original domain and integer code.
LOGBOOK.md:820:- DECISION: `OwnedVPNManagerRepository` remains the only ownership/schema authority and now hands out a session only from a freshly loaded exact-owned current manager. `VPNSessionController` retains no manager cache or forwarding state; iOS/macOS wrappers retain the fresh manager only to keep its exact public `NETunnelProviderSession` alive for the command/observer lifetime.
LOGBOOK.md:854:- SCHEMA: Provider stop metadata extends diagnostics v1 to 97 counters, 57 gauges, and 11 finite error codes across the same 10 domains. The schema still retains no endpoints, DNS names, traffic identifiers, secrets, configuration, localized errors, or free-form labels.
LOGBOOK.md:855:- COVERAGE: Shared tests run through iOS and macOS seams for all four commands, hostile/oversized/future/mutating inputs, duplicates, nil handlers, retirement, all raw Apple reasons, startup and cleanup deadlines, stop-wins-start, fatal handoff, deallocation, and two 100-cycle baselines. Existing coordinator tests retain every startup acquisition/cancellation point and route-clear uncertainty coverage.
LOGBOOK.md:866:- BASELINE: The fixture now tracks tasks, timers, sockets, channels, and retained dependencies separately. One hundred factory generations restore every counter plus the coordinator's internal task/resource footprint; thirty-two concurrent starts produce one usable publication, and thirty-two repeated stop/health race generations clean each owned resource exactly once.
LOGBOOK.md:871:- REGRESSION: `stop()` treated the coordinator's initial disconnected state as an idempotent no-op, so it retained the profile reference and left the one-shot generation startable after stop returned.
LOGBOOK.md:877:- REGRESSION: A mandatory-health callback could enter after the tracked startup child returned but before the outer `start()` continuation resumed. Because `startupTask` was still retained, the callback deferred cleanup; the outer continuation then cleared the handle and returned success without revalidating actor state, leaving the generation parked in stopping with retained resources.
LOGBOOK.md:883:- IMPLEMENTATION: `TunnelRuntimeCoordinator` owns one actor-serialized generation and a tracked startup task. It retains each successful acquisition before the next cancellation check, rejects repeat starts, discards mismatched-generation health events, and coalesces caller cancellation, provider stop, startup failure, and mandatory health loss through one shielded cleanup task.
LOGBOOK.md:884:- SAFETY: Settings are requested only after validated configuration, authenticated SSH, TCP readiness, SSH-only safe DNS readiness, pure packet-plane preparation, and mandatory health checks. Unknown apply failures are conservatively treated as an uncertain commit and cleared; definite non-commit skips clear. A clear failure publishes TCP/DNS false while truthfully retaining `routesInstalled=true` and `routeState=clearFailed`.
LOGBOOK.md:889:- REWORK: Component recorders now reserve one of 256 pending typed-update slots with a zero-timeout semaphore and enqueue on a private serial diagnostics lane. Snapshot construction can serialize on that lane without holding anything packet or SSH executors need; saturation increments one generation-scoped aggregate and retains no rejected label or value.
LOGBOOK.md:892:- REGRESSION: Populated recursive JSON and reflected-property allowlists freeze snapshot, histogram, bucket, and error shapes. Hostile private-field tokens, 10,000 distinct metrics/errors, queue saturation, and a deliberately paused snapshot prove redaction, bounded retention, and packet/SSH progress.
LOGBOOK.md:896:- DECISION: `RuntimeDiagnosticsStore` owns one bounded generation with 96 counters, 56 gauges, one cumulative DNS-latency histogram, and at most one cataloged error per each of 10 finite domains. Packet/HEV use its `TunnelMetrics` recorder, SSH uses the same recorder without lane identity, and coordinator/TCP/DNS/route/memory use typed finite-category updates; unknown free-form metric names are counted then discarded without retaining the label.
LOGBOOK.md:898:- PRIVACY: The default schema has no lane/run/flow IDs, DNS or destination fields, addresses, credentials, commands/stdin, payload content, or traffic samples. State transition times are monotonic process-uptime milliseconds; errors retain only validated domain/code; flow, memory, route, health, packet/byte, drop-reason, DNS-result, and SSH values are aggregates.
LOGBOOK.md:919:- SAFETY: Settings clear is called only after a committed or uncertain apply. A required failed/uncertain clear publishes capabilities false but truthfully retains routesInstalled=true with routeState=clearFailed; a clear that was unnecessary or confirmed publishes routesInstalled=false. Legacy version protocol v1 remains byte-exact while new M1 commands/snapshots use explicit schemas.
LOGBOOK.md:925:- BOUNDS: Swift and Go report the same 28,577 consumed bytes, 20-byte peak retained state, 4,096-byte peak allocated body, two maximum body allocations per case, 42 maximum processing iterations against a 43-iteration maximum ceiling, five maximum chunks, 96-byte diagnostics, and zero retained/outstanding body bytes after every terminal and reset path. Successful output records each exact seed ID, value, and semantic digest without payload content.
LOGBOOK.md:939:- RESOLUTION: Swift and Go now validate ATYP, recomputed HDRLEN, address and port bounds, nonzero port, and exact outer/MSGLEN arithmetic before applying either payload limit. Mirrored tables cover every structural stage at both 513-byte local-policy and 1473-byte protocol-violation declarations with zero decoded materialization; valid 513-byte and 1473-byte records retain their distinct reject-versus-close outcomes. Verification: relay protocol gate, 150 Swift tests, Go vet/tests with 91.3% coverage, 1,135,854 fuzz executions, strict formatting, core-boundary guard, and diff validation all pass.
LOGBOOK.md:948:- IMPLEMENTATION: Swift and Go now encode the four-byte big-endian body length plus type/flags/association ID as separate header/payload write slices, and decode arbitrary partial/coalesced stream reads while retaining at most one negotiated frame plus the fixed prefix. Prefix bounds are checked before the first body allocation; generated message metadata drives direction, association-ID, fixed-payload, reserved-flag, and negotiated DNS-priority validation.
LOGBOOK.md:949:- DECISION: One `consume` call is transactional when a later coalesced frame is session-fatal: frames completed earlier in that same call are not returned or counted, while frames returned by earlier calls remain counted. This keeps the throwing Swift API and mirrored Go behavior deterministic and preserves `inputBytes = outputBytes + retainedBytes + discardedBytes` after both success and failure.
LOGBOOK.md:951:- REWORK: The Swift codec suite type is `RelayProtocolByteCodecTests`, so the frozen `swift test --filter RelayProtocol` step now selects it. `make relay-protocol-check` visibly runs the envelope suite and passes 29 tests across the generated-constants, handshake, and codec suites while retaining the mirrored Go smoke package.
LOGBOOK.md:963:- SECURITY: Both peers expose only finite local code/phase/scope/disposition diagnostics; unknown statuses and attacker bytes are not retained or formatted. Feature selection is the requested/supported intersection, and peer `maxFrame` is range-checked and locally bounded before producing `RelayEffectiveLimits`.
LOGBOOK.md:971:- VERIFICATION: full gate PASS (double regen byte-identical, checked-in match, digest OK, stale/manual-edit self-test OK); live demo: hand-editing 1472→1473 in generated Go fails `check` exit 1; `swift test` 117/117; `check-core-boundaries` PASS. Evidence: board outcome `TASK-260715-2azda7_results.md`, demo diffs in `.temp/relay-protocol-demo/`.
LOGBOOK.md:989:- ANOMALY: Board resource `TASK-260715-111tde_foundation-blocked-analysis.md` is 0 bytes despite its "retained for provenance" description; content survives in task notes and LOGBOOK 1510. Non-blocking; recommend delete-or-restore.
LOGBOOK.md:994:- DECISION: Canonical JSON at `Protocol/Relay/relay-v1.schema.json` generates checked-in Swift/Go values only; handwritten Swift in `ReluxTunnelCore/RelayProtocol` and Go in `relay/internal/protocol` own behavior. `make relay-protocol-generate` is the sole regeneration command and `make relay-protocol-check` owns deterministic double-generation, drift/manual-edit failure, compilation, and schema-negative gates. No Swift/Go FFI or runtime schema parser is permitted.
LOGBOOK.md:1023:- FIX: The verified HEV build script is rendered in memory from manifest minima and executed without modifying the pinned checkout or C sources. Every retained HEV slice now targets iOS/tvOS 18.0 or macOS 15.0; ReluxLibSSH2 triples, OpenSSL flags, CMake targets, artifacts, and locks now target iOS 18.0/macOS 15.0. Inspection rejects unmodeled XCFramework slices.
LOGBOOK.md:1034:- FIX: The fault and 100-cycle real-HEV regressions no longer use `openDescriptorCount() == baseline` as a pass/fail condition. Each harness instead records its own boundary stop, live SOCKS channels, packet-flow reads/queues, bridge endpoint-close lifecycle stages, and cleanup-close errors; the process-global descriptor baseline/observed delta is retained only in failure diagnostics.
LOGBOOK.md:1049:- ROOT CAUSE / DECISION: `boundary.stop()` was a product double invocation (`requestStop()` plus `waitForReturn()`), not a bad integration expectation. A lock-coalesced stop task now invokes the boundary once and lets both lifecycle paths await the same operation; unit and real-HEV cycle tests assert one start/one stop.
LOGBOOK.md:1058:- OPTIONS: Preserve unmodified HEV by capturing statistics while main is still active (immediately before quit, plus an explicit strategy for spontaneous return), add a wrapper-owned live snapshot to the native runtime seam, or explicitly remove completed-run HEV counters from the acceptance contract. Recommendation: retain the counters and revise the runtime seam to snapshot before HEV fini; do not weaken the integration assertions or patch the pinned HEV binary.
LOGBOOK.md:1129:- IMPLEMENTATION: Added `relay-portable-assets` / `inspect-assets`, which requires a caller-owned total bundle budget and emits a path-free four-asset report only after exact layout/name, regular executable mode, raw format/machine, Go CPU metadata, linkage, minimum runtime, dynamic-library, debug-section, size, SHA-256, and privacy checks. An over-budget report is retained before the command fails; no default budget silently creates product policy.
LOGBOOK.md:1130:- VERIFICATION: A detached clean worktree at `58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096` built exactly Darwin/Linux amd64/arm64 with pinned Go 1.26.5, `--require-clean`, release linker flags, protocol v1 identity `0.1.0`, and source epoch `1784656987`. The four files total 10,259,950 bytes and are retained in task outcome archive `TASK-260715-24icoz_portable-relay-assets.tar.gz`; each is mode 0755, stripped with no DWARF companion, and passed format/linkage/metadata/privacy inspection.
LOGBOOK.md:1132:- ANOMALY: Two concurrent local `task-board resource add` mutations copied both payloads but preserved only one progress reference, leaving the results file orphaned. The exact orphan was deleted and re-added sequentially from its retained task-scoped source; `task-board validate` is the closure gate. Board resource mutations should remain sequential in local-file mode.
LOGBOOK.md:1163:- DECISION: ADR-014 remains open. Both candidates retain identical host-key, window, sustained 5 GiB rekey, scale (through 1,000 channels), cancellation, algorithm, extension-build, memory, and physical-size gates. Unknowns are named experiments in `.research/260720_task-260715-28ok1k-ssh-engine-candidate-audit.md`; no missing capability was waived.
LOGBOOK.md:1185:- DECISION NEEDED: Either approve an additional injectable `udp-copy-buffer-nums` baseline of `1` or `2` so the effective stack remains 24576, explicitly accept 35480 as the effective stack while retaining 24576 only as an input, or revise the no-patch constraint. Recommendation: approve `2` as an explicit M0 measurement input; do not patch HEV or claim that 24576 is effective while the parser overrides it.
LOGBOOK.md:1194:- DECISION: ADR-019 uses locally source-rebuilt static XCFramework SwiftPM `binaryTarget`s for custom-build C graphs behind named native adapter modules; source-reviewable ReluxNIOSSH stays a pinned source package. `ReluxTunnelCore` retains no native dependency.
LOGBOOK.md:1207:- FINDING: cgo-free Linux outputs are fully static without musl or glibc; Darwin outputs necessarily retain `libSystem` and `libresolv`. The selected Go toolchain raises the remote macOS floor to 12.0; the project sets a conservative Linux 4.4 floor.
LOGBOOK.md:1227:### 0420 — PacketFlow read gate retains late-callback tombstones (TASK-260720-9xy8yx)
LOGBOOK.md:1252:- VERIFICATION: Independent `--no-hardlinks` detached-clone validation at `7dc73ac6e7325f86a4a178a0558619f0fc9d1490` passed the repository credential-free matrix (exit 0, 417.04s), strict formatting, 89.96% product-line coverage, exact macOS graph, double generation, unsigned Debug/Release bundle/linkage inspection, relay checksums, and pinned legacy regression. No signing, installation, application/provider launch, VPN preference/tunnel, route, or DNS operation ran.
LOGBOOK.md:1264:- VERDICT: Changes requested. Preserve the actor-atomic check/register and exact cleanup assertions, but make readiness a terminal event state that also completes waiters on command startup failure/cancellation, and add deterministic regression coverage proving that path cannot hang or retain a waiter.
LOGBOOK.md:1273:- VERIFICATION: Four-worker loaded harness stress, an independent clean 446-test full suite, clean 446-test coverage suite, strict recursive Swift format, core boundaries, diff check, and board validation all exited 0. Signal exit 143, empty output, zero directory/socket residue, and exactly-one managed-task cancellation remain asserted; the injected startup failure terminates with its exact diagnostic and zero retained waiters.
LOGBOOK.md:1302:- ROOT CAUSE: The replacement state retained only an enum and discarded the initially observed directory identity. If stale directory A was renamed aside and foreign directory B appeared before publication, generation could exchange and delete B.
LOGBOOK.md:1304:- VERIFICATION: Three exact regressions cover replacement immediately after observation, at `before_publish`, and after the final identity check. All preserve B's exact inode and marker, retain A outside the destination, and leave no owned staging. The 24-test Python suite, 4 Swift manifest tests, accepted-archive bundle generation/check, byte-identical double regeneration, Black, Python compile, and diff checks pass.
LOGBOOK.md:1309:- VERIFICATION: The exact post-open cleanup race moves stale A aside and installs foreign B at the staging name. Generation fails, B retains its exact inode and marker, A survives, and the published bundle validates. Normal cleanup, symlink refusal, interruption recovery, all 26 Python tests, 4 Swift manifest tests, accepted-archive bundle check, Black, Python compile, and diff checks pass.
LOGBOOK.md:1312:- FINDING: The first runtime gate sent SIGTERM and immediately closed stdin. On a fresh pinned Go 1.26.5 build, EOF occasionally won the race and the relay exited 0 before its signal owner produced the required exit 130; an older retained artifact happened to pass, so a single green smoke did not expose the harness defect.
LOGBOOK.md:1314:- VERIFICATION: The exact fresh-build failure is retained in `.temp/TASK-260715-mocqmr/native-darwin-arm64-current/report.json`. After the fix, eight repeated fixture signal checks and twelve consecutive full native Darwin arm64 gates passed with exit 130. The pinned four-target build and manifest verification, Go tests/vet, release-tool regressions, actionlint, supply-chain audit, toolchain check, and 84%+ affected Python coverage pass.
LOGBOOK.md:1317:- FINDING: Independent review proved that a relay fixture could create a new session, become reparented, write under a shared temporary directory, and survive while the old gate passed. Direct-child sampling and scanning only the private runtime directory did not establish either process lineage cleanup or a system-write boundary. Reports also retained emulated executable paths and omitted already-observed exit codes on mismatch paths.
LOGBOOK.md:1322:- FINDING: Existing double-build executable and protocol-test bytes were identical, but Syft 1.48.0 emitted a wall-clock `creationInfo.created` value and random UUID suffix in `documentNamespace` for each SPDX file. Those eight metadata differences cascaded into different four-entry manifest and checksum bytes, while the comparator checked only executables and incorrectly passed.
LOGBOOK.md:1329:- ANOMALY: The historical recipe predates the safe `archive-assets` subcommand. The operator procedure uses the current non-byte-affecting, ownership-safe archive writer only after both four-target builds, then makes the retained archive comparison authoritative instead of presenting the missing historical command as runnable.
LOGBOOK.md:1330:- VERIFICATION: Two independent no-local/no-hardlink clones rebuilt all four accepted executables and normalized archives. Both archives were byte-identical to each other and to the retained `TASK-260715-24icoz` archive at SHA-256 `1f0ba226ed591d1baf5f9464b33e45b7658a33bf5a1a114e77b6d22d3d9eef4e`; trusted bundle generation/check passed and its manifest was byte-identical to the current bundled manifest. No signing, installation, application/provider launch, VPN, route, interface, packet-filter, DNS, or remote execution occurred.
LOGBOOK.md:1332:- RESOLUTION: The runbook now limits the historical claim to the exact executables/archive and deterministically regenerated trusted application manifest, requires immutable retention for old release-builder metadata, and routes every new candidate through the accepted `TASK-260715-1q03sa` normalization recipe. Both clone outputs are staged below one invoked checkout's `.build/relay` root before the exact 11-release-file plus four-protocol-test comparison. It separately identifies `relux-relay-manifest-v1.json` as unbundled release-builder/native-smoke evidence and `relux-relay-assets-v1.json` as the generated application-bundle/rollback manifest.
LOGBOOK.md:1334:- UPDATE-ORDER ANOMALY: Rework 02 confirmed that the original step 6 could not run `relay-supply-chain-generate` for a changed source/version/archive while step 9 still retained the old asset contract. `validate_config()` requires the supply-chain source revision/version and accepted archive task/resource/SHA to equal `asset-bundle-source-v1.json`, and generation then rewrites that contract's supply-chain link and the Swift catalog. The Swift acceptance test also pins the accepted archive and build identity.
LOGBOOK.md:1343:- VALIDATION ANOMALY: A post-rework full `swift test` run exited `1` because the unrelated libssh2 `clientAndServerRekey` M0 gate did not observe `.closed` before its assertion; the run otherwise reached all 455 tests and reported the existing 25 known ReluxNIOSSH issues. An immediate exact `mandatoryGate` rerun passed all 18 argument rows (exit `0`, nine known unavailable-adapter issues), so the failure is retained as a transport-suite timing anomaly rather than attributed to the UI-test infrastructure.
LOGBOOK.md:1349:- VERIFICATION: Six focused fake-only Swift suites passed 53 tests. The real coordinator boundary rejects every invalid profile class before injected Keychain/network fakes; all nine `SSHHostKeyDecision` cases traverse the candidate-neutral transport seam with `hostPolicy -> credentialLookup -> authentication` only on accepted paths. One independently owned lifecycle registry retains concrete task, connection, observer, and callback tokens across all 16 bounded iterations; gated cancellation observes all four non-zero, and balanced teardown restores the same registry baseline after success, every rejecting host decision, an injected thrown policy, and cancellation without assigning counters to zero. Three additional cleanup/redaction matrix repetitions passed; captured-log prohibited-data, test-source live-Security, public-fixture, live-network, and self-reset-counter scans returned no matches. Coverage reported 87.75% affected lines and 87.04% affected functions; strict Swift format, core boundaries, and diff checks exited 0. The first focused compile exited 1 on a missing explicit `return`; the corrected rerun and every subsequent gate exited 0. No real Keychain, SSH connection, NetworkExtension runtime, VPN configuration, route, DNS, interface, or packet-filter operation ran.
